# A network card that appears while the box runs is offered to the dataplane
# (#453). Only a PCI card: a veth, a bridge or a tap has no PCI parent. The
# unit, not RUN directly: udev kills a RUN program after a few seconds, and
# the attach talks to the dataplane.
#
# add AND move. Measured in a KVM guest with `udevadm monitor` over a card
# added by device_add: the add event carried SYSTEMD_WANTS, then udev renamed
# eth0 to ens20 and emitted a move, and systemd started nothing - the unit ran
# only when the event was triggered again by hand. The move is what systemd
# acts on for a renamed card. Our own rename to xdp-* is excluded below, and
# the rename back in restart-dataplane finds the card already on the
# dataplane, or the dataplane not answering, and leaves it.
ACTION=="add|move", SUBSYSTEM=="net", SUBSYSTEMS=="pci", KERNEL!="xdp-*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="prisma-routing-hot-card@$name.service"
